AB  - The lab test showed that there were not much differences in the toxicity to 3rd-4th instar larvae of D. punctatus between M. anisopliae and B. bassiana at 25deg C. The median lethal concentration of M. anisopliae was 6.38X10~(8) spores·L~(-1), and the median lethal time was 8.60-15.19 days for the concentration of 1.0X10~(11)-1.0X10~(7) spores·L~(-1). The median lethal concentration of B. bassiana was 5.06X10~(8) spores·L~(-1), and the median lethal time was 7.80-14.79 days for the concentration of 1.0X10~(11)-1.0X10~(7) spores·L~(-1). The strain of M. anisopliae was more tolerant to high temperature and drought than B. bassiana. At high temperature or low humidity, the pathogenicity on D. punctatus was superior to that by B. bassiana.
