AB  - Neoaplectaua carpocapsae developed and reproduced in armyworm hosts infected with a granulosis virus (GV). Macerated tissues of dauer juveniles from GV-infected hosts had sufficient GV to infect 1st and 2nd instar armyworms. Electron-microscope examination of dauer juveniles and adult female nematodes confirmed the presence of GV in the lumen of the intestine. No GV was observed in other tissues of the nematode.
